outcomes:
  desired:
    - Every markdown file under the six content roots becomes exactly one route with a lowercase address under its own section, its doc name in the file's own case for labels, and the commit hash that last touched it, or a named uncommitted marker for an untracked file. Any route can be looked up by section and name regardless of case.
    - "Routes are ordered deterministically: sections in the site's category order with methodology first, each section's index first, then alphabetically by lowercase address. One build discovers the doc set once, and every page in that build sees the same routes."
    - Each route carries its first-published date and its true last-modified date, the last commit touching its source in shared version history, so the date a doc page shows, the sitemap, its structured data and the feed all agree.
